DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions calculate the inverse hyperbolic tangent of _x; that is
       the value whose hyperbolic tangent is _x.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return the inverse hyperbolic tangent of _x.

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is +0 (-0), +0 (-0) is returned.

       If _x is +1 or -1,  a  pole  error  occurs,  and  the  functions  return
       HHUUGGEE__VVAALL,  HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF,  or  HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL, respectively, with the mathemati‐
       cally correct sign.

       If the absolute value of _x is greater than 1, a  domain  error  occurs,
       and a NaN is returned.

EERRRROORRSS
       See  mmaatthh__eerrrroorr(7) for information on how to determine whether an error
       has occurred when calling these functions.

       The following errors can occur:

       Domain error: _x less than -1 or greater than +1
              _e_r_r_n_o is set  to  EEDDOOMM.   An  invalid  floating‐point  exception
              (FFEE__IINNVVAALLIIDD) is raised.

       Pole error: _x is +1 or -1
              _e_r_r_n_o  is set to EERRAANNGGEE (but see BUGS).  A divide‐by‐zero float‐
              ing‐point exception (FFEE__DDIIVVBBYYZZEERROO) is raised.

